     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Governance for tobacco control was strengthened through UNDP support in 12 countries, among them Cabo Verde, Chad, Colombia El Salvador, Georgia, Jordan, Madagascar, Nepal and Zambia. 

Tobacco control investment cases were launched in Armenia, Eswatini, Suriname and Tunisia. The first country-specific Tobacco control SDG briefs were launched in Zambia and Cabo Verde. 

Tobacco control governance capacity building provided to 11 countries through support on WHO FCTC Article 5 (national tobacco control strategies, multisectoral coordination and conflict-of-interest prevention and management. 
Eleven new FCTC 2030 countries were added in 2021 as a third phase of the project. 

The activities undertaken in these 12 countries have been linked to more than 30 specific changes to laws or policies that strengthen tobacco control in the project countries.</narrative>
